Objects and References

References
A reference is a variable type that refers to an object.
	A reference may be thought of as storing the memory address of an object.
	Variables of a class data type (and array types, discussed elsewhere) are reference variables.

The new operator allocates memory for an object

Declaration:
	TimeHrMin travelTime; //declares a reference variable with an unknown value
Object Creation:
	travelTime = new TimeHrMin(); //sets travelTime to refer to a new TimeHrMin object in memory
	
The reference variable declaration and object creation may be combined into a single statement:
	TimeHrMin travelTime = new TimeHrMin();

---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Multiple reference variables may refer to the same object.

DriveTime timeRoute1 = new DriveTime();
DriveTime timeRoute2;
DriveTime bestRoute;

timeRoute2 = new DriveTime();
bestRoute = timeRoute1;


